From 857295d6ec0b8b2ce9e1219c52830e20b5d4d98d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:59:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Position limits; shared-domain distribution strips

TE filled 38/40 FLEX slots. Not a variance bug -- the simulator is unbiased at
every position (sim mean == projection to 0.0%) and TE ceiling/$1k (4.26) is
indistinguishable from WR (4.25). It is structural: the roster consumes 3 WR
and 2 RB before FLEX but only 1 TE, so with similar value curves the best
REMAINING player is a TE nearly every time. position_limits={'TE':1} costs 2.3
projected points per lineup and raises N_eff 9.2 -> 10.0.

Distribution strips were binned over each lineup's own range and normalised to
its own height, so forty different distributions rendered as forty identical
bell curves. They now share a domain and a density scale across the set, so
position reads as mean and width as spread.
